From: Audit Hub <audit-hub@audit-hub.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:02:42 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] feat(audit): ship the Audit Hub connector, installed
 and off

Audit Hub keeps a tamper-evident log of a project's security events,
alerts on them and answers "my account's security". Its connectors are
vendored source (`pnpm connector add` in Audit Hub's repository): this
adds both, the API's (apps/api/src/audit/, its outbox tables and their
migration) and the SPA's (apps/web/src/audit/), with every integration
point. Unless all five AUDIT_HUB_* connection variables are set, it
stays off: nothing is recorded or sent, its routes answer 404, the boot
is unaffected.

On, each flow records its event in the transaction of its change: the
sign-in (through onCreated) and its failures, a disabled account or a
required password included, sign-outs, session theft, revokeAll,
password resets and changes, email changes, sign-ups, invitations
(revoke now runs in a transaction for it), role changes, disabling and
enabling, required password changes, deletions (which Audit Hub erases),
admins reading other people's records, cross-origin refusals and
rate-limited auth requests. A person is named by their name; their email
leaves only as a keyed pseudonym, and a phone, where one is known, only as
its last four digits. Each request's client hints go with it (the real
browser and system). Audit
Hub's response actions (revoke_sessions, require_password_change and
disable_account, each listed in AUDIT_HUB_RESPONSE_ACTIONS) do what an
admin does here, under the same rules. The web app reports CSP
violations, refused ways back and ended sessions through a lazy chunk
loaded only when the API says the connector is on, and the account page
lists the person's own activity. AuditErasureService asks Audit Hub to
erase a user: their personal data, or their events too.

The revoke helpers now answer how many sessions they ended. The
variables are in the env schema, .env.example and docs/environment.md;
docs/security.md#audit-hub, manual 11.6 (both languages), a runbook and
its alerts (ApiAuditBacklog, ApiAuditRejections, ApiAuditHubRefused)
with their promtool tests describe it. The reporter has a budget of its
own; the total rose from 159 to 160 kB, measured.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
